boarding this london-bound train  36-year-old darren pencil  who just minutes later would be involved  in a deadly confrontation  with a fellow passenger that man i.t  consultant lee pomeroy boarded shortly  after  along with his 14 year old son it's just  after 1 pm  on the 4th of january this year almost  immediately  darren pencil and mr pomeroy were  involved in a heated argument  as the train pulled out of gilford  station  pencil accusing lee pomeroy of blocking  the aisle according to witnesses  there's no sound on these security  camera images but the fact they're  arguing is clear  an old bailly jury watched as pencil  moved off  into a neighboring carriage mr pomeroy  followed  and the pair continued their row  moments later the argument turned  violent in  images shown to the jury but too graphic  to be released publicly  the victim is seen being stabbed 18  times  in just 25 seconds before the accused  left the train at clandon station a  british transport police detective  described it as a quick and frenzied  attack  husband and wife christopher and megan  feiberg  witnessed the escalating dispute and  fled the carriage but not before seeing  the two men grab  each other's collars megan feiberg said  the white man  was pretty angry a video testimony from  the victim's fourteen-year-old son was  played in court  he said his father was tall so could  look pretty menacing  that he heard pencil tell his dad to get  off at the next station  which he perceived as a threat the  defendant's girlfriend chelsea mitchell  is also on trial but denies assisting an  offender  darren pencil admits possessing a knife  but has pleaded not guilty to murdering  lee pomeroy  mark white sky news
 

